We’re organizing a citywide donation drive and need to pick which potential drop-off boxes to install and then decide which installed box each donor will go to. Each possible box costs money to place, and each donor incurs some detour to reach the box they’re assigned to, so the trick is to keep the total cost down by adding all the installation fees and every donor’s extra travel; a lower total means a better rollout. Also, every donor must be routed to one single box that’s actually been installed — no duplicates, no unassigned donors, and nobody should be told to use a box that wasn’t put out. The specific locations, costs, and donor positions are listed below.

